      "Therefore 2a+6b≡90/7 (mod m), and since n is the answer, n≡90/7 (mod m)."
    ],
    "error_step": "But we must have this as an integer — so the value $ \frac{90}{7} $ must be an integer in modulo $ m $.",
    "error_reason": "In modular arithmetic, 90/7 means 90 times the inverse of 7 modulo m, so it is already an integer residue class modulo m, not a rational number that must simplify to an integer. The later conclusion 90/7≡12 is therefore unjustified.",
    "new_direction": "Use the self-reference n=m−1 and substitute m−1≡90/7 (mod m) to derive a divisibility condition on m."
  }
